            "review_title": "Review at Yunka - Nikkei Cuisine & Cocktails",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nUnique Jap-Peruvian cuisine, Love the glowing bar and chill lounge vibes\nJun 2025 • Family\nHere with the fam after a great year end performance over at Saigon Opera House.\n\nWhile dishes here are not the cheapest in town, the:\n- awesome location,\n(hundred-metre vicinity of best malls e.g. Saigon Centre and hotels e.g. Hyatt in town),\n- great vibes,\n(the couches and indoor-outdoor greenery vibes with chill music)\n- unique and delicious cuisine...\n(the well-known yummy Jap dishes elevated with South American i.e. Peruvian touch)\n...all the above totally makes the price worth it here.\n\nThe twirly lit staircase with trendy vertical orange subway tiles backsplash, leading up to the second floor of lantern-lit red ceilings and the show-stopping glowing bar in the center simply sets anyone up in a chill mood. Love it.\n\nAlso it was so fun trying out the flavours of everything we ordered:\n- Ebi Mentaiko - love the sauce and Pandano cheese\n- Acevichada Maki - this feels regular but I guess the sauce made a diff\n- Corn Ribs - with Huancaina sauce!\n- Tacos Nikkei - ceviche in tacos\n- Moriawase Ceviche - seafood, tiger milk, ikura, chives oil. We Googled Tiger milk.\n- Chaufa Yunka - pork belly with fried rice and roasted banana!!\n- Amazonico - jungle Peruvian choc sounds way more fun than other chocs\n\nMost bars serve snack-ish bar grubs, but this bar serves honestly superb tasting and actually filling food.\nRead more\nWritten September 29, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
